return {
["13:00"]={"That day it was \003one o’clock\004 before John and Roger rowed across and went up to Dixon’s farm for the milk and a new supply of eggs and butter.","Swallows and Amazons","Arthur Ransome"},
["13:01"]={"He heard a distant confused yelling. Harse and the cop? But it didn’t matter. The only thing that mattered was getting to the Nexus Point at \003one minute past one\004.","Survival Kit","Frederik Pohl"},
["13:05"]={"At \003five past one\004 Alleyn opened the outer door, knocked his pipe out on the edge of the stone step,and remained staring out on to the drive.","A Man Lay Dead","Ngaio Marsh"},
["13:06"]={"And then at precisely \00313 hours and 6 minutes\004 — confusion broke out in the rectangle.","We","Yevgeny Zamyatin"},
["13:07"]={"Dr. Nexa accepted her forced surrender to the inevitable with a greater modicum of grace. She looked at Nurse L’Kem and said, pointing to the human, the Bolian, and then the Zaldan, “Time of death for Lieutenant Hutchinson, \0031307 hours\004.”","Star Trek: Destiny #3: Lost Souls","David Mack"},
["13:08"]={"\00313:08 GMT\004\nLamont and Jackie had joined the team in the canteen for lunch, where the babble of expectant chatter revealed how eager they all were to get on with the job.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["13:09"]={"At \003nine minutes past one\004, a pair of horses approached (not from the city, from which direction Krieger had expected her to come, but from the Desert, which lay, vast and largely uncharted, out to the West and South-West of the city.)","Tortured Souls: The Legend of Primordium","Clive Barker"},
["13:10"]={"It was at \003ten minutes past one\004 by Bond’s watch when, at the high table, the whole pattern of play suddenly altered.","Casino Royale","Ian Fleming"},
["13:11"]={"I pursued my inquiries at the other stations along the line an’ I found there was a gentleman wi’ a bicycle tuk the \0031:11\004 train at Girvan.","Five Red Herrings","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["13:12"]={"At \003twelve minutes past one\004 the adjutant, Wilde, and myself sat down to lunch.\n“The colonel said he wouldn’t be late—but we needn’t wait,” said the adjutant.","Pushed and the Return Push","George Herbert Fosdike Nichols"},
["13:13"]={"There it is! There it is! shouted the Professor. “Now for the centre of the globe!” he added in Danish.\nI looked at Hans. “Forüt!” was his tranquil answer.\n“Forward!” replied my uncle. It was \003thirteen minutes past one\004.","Journey to the Center of the Earth","Jules Verne"},
["13:14"]={"Agent Brooks pulled out a small notepad and flipped to a page. “On September 26th at \0031:14 pm\004 Central Standard Time, Oakly Acadia Laveau’s biological tracker registered an error code. Afterward, all biological activity ceased.”","Extinction Island","Janice Boekhoff"},
["13:15"]={"Monsieur has well slept this morning, he said, smiling.\n“What o’clock is it, Victor?” asked Dorian Gray, sleepily.\n“\003One hour and a quarter\004, monsieur.”","The Picture of Dorian Gray","Oscar Wilde"},
["13:16"]={"And the first stop had been at \0031:16 p.m.\004 which was 17 minutes later.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["13:17"]={"\0031:17 pm\004. An arrest is made at Bristol Airport and police confirm that they’ve detained a person in connection with the investigation.","What She Knew","Gilly MacMillan"},
["13:18"]={"\003One eighteen\004 exactly. Was she stupid enough to head inside? Or wasn’t she? We’ll know before long, When the dead are carried out.","The Terrorist, He Watches","Wislawa Szymborska"},
["13:19"]={"It was \003past one in the afternoon\004 when the servant waked her and announced that M. Artynov had called. She dressed quickly and went down into the drawing-room.","The Party and Other Stories","Anton Pavlovich Chekhov"},
["13:20"]={"Gerard and I took the launch to Greenwich and had a pub lunch at the Trafalgar Tavern, but we didn’t leave here until \003twenty past one\004.","Original Sin","P.D. James"},
["13:21"]={"\0031:21 P.M.\004\nVance was moving as fast as he could and watching as the helicopter—now about a thousand yards from the pad—began its final approach.\nFriend or foe?","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["13:22"]={"It was \0031:22\004 when we found Dad’s grave.","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer"},
["13:23"]={"And when we got to Swindon Mother had keys to the house and we went in and she said, “Hello?” but there was no one there because it was \0031:23 p.m.\004","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["13:24"]={"Littell checked his watch — \0031:24 p.m\004 — Littell grabbed the phone by the bed.","The Cold Six Thousand","James Ellroy"},
["13:25"]={"I’d really have liked to, I told her, if it weren’t for the things I had in the dryer. I cast an eye at my watch. \003One-twenty-five\004. The dryer had already stopped.","Hard-Boiled Wonderland and the End of the World","Haruki Murakami"},
["13:27"]={"At \00313:27\004 on that self-same Friday, 20 June, seventy-two hours before his disappearance, Adria Daedalus Sorra, man-about-town, disc jockey and student of philosophy, careened up the stairs with his skateboard.","The Serpent Papers","Jessica Cornwell"},
["13:28"]={"At \00313:28\004 Van walked into the Korvel Mercantile Tower, then took the lift to the third floor. From there, he made his way along the southern corridor to the open door beside the IIS spelled out in silvered letters on the taupe plaster wall. He stepped inside.","The Ethos Effect","L.E. Modesitt Jr."},
["13:29"]={"Monday, April 6\n\0031:29 P.M.\004\nAs she hung up, Ally wondered again what she was getting into. But she did want to meet this miracle worker. The kind of thing Van de Vliet was talking about sounded as much like science fiction as anything she’d ever heard.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["13:30"]={"Lupin not having come down, I went up again at \003half-past one\004, and said we dined at two; he said he “would be there.”","The Diary of a Nobody","George and Weedon Grossmith"},
["13:31"]={"Raymond came back with Masson \003around one-thirty\004. His arm was bandaged up and he had an adhesive plaster on the corner of his mouth. The doctor had told him it was nothing, but Raymond looked pretty grim. Masson tried to make him laugh. But he still wouldn’t say anything.","The Stranger","Albert Camus"},
["13:32"]={"I sat down on the couch again and looked at my watch It was \003one thirty-two\004. I shut my eyes and focused on a spot in my head. My mind a total blank, I gave myself up to the sands of time and let the flow take me wherever it wanted.","Blind Willow, Sleeping Woman","Haruki Murakami"},
["13:33"]={"He waited for the green light to show and then opened the door again on to the now empty cargo hold. ‘… \003one … thirty-three\004 … and fifty seconds.’ Very nice.","So Long, and Thanks for All the Fish","Douglas Adams"},
["13:34"]={"At the third stroke it will be …\nHe tiptoed out and returned to the control cabin.\n“… \003one … thirty-four\004 and twenty seconds.”\nThe voice sounded as clear as if he was hearing it over a phone in London, which he wasn’t, not by a long way.","So Long, and Thanks for All the Fish","Douglas Adams"},
["13:35"]={"Fletcher checked his watch again. It was \0031:35 P.M.\004 He sighed and asked the receptionist if he could use the washroom.","Sons of Fortune","Jeffrey Archer"},
["13:36"]={"Eli came at \0031:36 p.m.\004 I knew the exact time because I was sitting and staring at the analog clock on my phone when the doorbell rang.","His Only Wife","Peace Adzo Medie"},
["13:38"]={"According to the digital readout inside my helmet, it was only \00313:38\004 LT. The news that I wouldn’t have to devote another three hours to painstaking cleanup should have cheered me considerably; instead, it rendered me about twenty times more suspicious.","Sunday Night Yams at Minnie and Earl’s","Adam-Troy Castro"},
["13:39"]={"And it was now \0031:39 p.m.\004 which was 23 minutes after the stop, which meant that we would be at the sea if the train didn’t go in a big curve. But I didn’t know if it went in a big curve.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["13:40"]={"Glancing at his watch, Chandler-Powell saw that it was \003one-forty\004. Perhaps he should now have a word with the Bostocks, who were closeted in the kitchen. He needed to check again that Kimberly had fully recovered and that they were giving thought to food.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["13:41"]={"I will begin a few minutes before the leak started — at \0031:41 pm\004, 13:41 Universal Time — one hour and twenty three minutes ago. At that point the chief flight engineer was attempting to discover why the engines had gone into automatic shutdown.","Bones Burnt Black","Stephen Euin Cobb"},
["13:42"]={"The last note was recorded at \0031:42 pm\004: G.M. on site at H-by; will take over the matter.","The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo","Stieg Larsson"},
["13:43"]={"There’s a train at \003seventeen minutes to two\004, said Didier. He blessed himself and got to his feet. He hesitated.\n“What’s the matter?”\n“Shouldn’t we say goodbye to Grandpa? He usually has a cheque for me.”","The Public Prosecutor","Jef Geeraerts"},
["13:44"]={"By good luck, the next train was due at \003forty-four minutes past one\004, and arrived at Yateland (the next station) ten minutes afterward.","Mr. Policeman and the Cook","Wilkie Collins"},
["13:45"]={"Let us know the moment Harvey leaves his box. My guess is that around \0031:45\004 he’ll come and look at the runners and riders for the two o’clock, so that gives us a clear hour.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["13:46"]={"PAUL: I noticed Malatarsis right after Mama called me. At \0031346 hours\004 on Thursday the twenty-fourth. Brett was killed at least fourteen hours later, in the wee hours of the twenty-fifth.","Jack the Bodiless","Julian May"},
["13:47"]={"Poppy was sprawled on Brianne’s bed, applying black mascara to her stubby lashes. Brianne was sitting at her desk, trying to complete an essay before the 2 pm deadline. It was \0031:47 pm\004.","The Woman Who Went to Bed for a Year","Sue Townsend"},
["13:49"]={"The bookstall clerk had seen the passenger in grey pass the bookstall at \0031:49\004, in the direction of the exit.","Five Red Herrings","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["13:50"]={"The best train of the day was the \003one-fifty\004 from Paddington which reached Polgarwith just after seven o’clock.","The Cornish Mystery","Agatha Christie"},
["13:51"]={"Which meant that now, at \0031:51 p.m.\004, lower Manhattan was a nightmare. Wall Street had been cordoned off for blocks in each direction. Foot police redirected traffic on Broadway, blowing whistles and gesturing impatiently.","Brilliance","Marcus Sakey"},
["13:52"]={"I came to your door to tell you. It is near to your luncheon hour. Yes; \003eight minutes to two\004. Vivian will be at luncheon. I don’t lunch, but I don’t mind going in. I must not let him slip through my fingers.","The Rose and the Key","Joseph Sheridan Le Fanu"},
["13:53"]={"Mr. Jackson, exclaimed Mr. Rossiter. “I really must ask you to be good enough to come in from your lunch at the proper time. It was fully \003seven minutes to two\004 when you returned, and—”","Psmith in the City","P.G. Wodehouse"},
["13:54"]={"At the moment museum officials do not believe anything was stolen from the collection. The museum and church, which are popular tourist attractions, will be closed to the public until further notice.\n\0031:54 PM\004 - 05/05/2014","The Catacombs","Jeremy Bates"},
["13:55"]={"At \0031:55\004 he returned to the insurance records until the fifteen-minute tea break at four o’clock, which was another ritual occasion for two more cigarettes.","Broken Routine","Jeffrey Archer"},
["13:57"]={"It was \003three minutes to two\004. “I hope you can catch him, then. Thank you. I really appreciate it.”","Urban Shaman","C.E. Murphy"},
["13:58"]={"Promptly at \003two minutes to two\004 that afternoon, the two majors presented themselves to General Austin’s temporary secretary at his away-from-Pentagon office.","Steel Tiger","Mark Berent"},
["13:59"]={"We had lunch at \003approximately two in the afternoon\004. Don Miguel rested his plate on a kerosene crate, I sat at the corner of a table covered with books, the fat woman was in the kitchen and Don Gaetano at the counter.","The rabid toy","Roberto Arlt"},
